Well, Damerell has started his usual descent, when
in heated discussions, from modest use of reason to
pure invective spewing bully mode, ignoring every
valid point made by his opponent in an attempt at
"total victory".

Meanwhile, the topic of discussion, whether to lob a
projectile at one oncoming opponent or rush toward
that opponent to accomplish one melee before another
melee begins, totally ignores NetHack wisdom by now
written in stone.

If you are in danger of being put into melee against
multiple monsters who collectively stand some chance
of nerfing your PC, the right answer is neither to
use "ranged, then melee" or "run to attempt faster
melee with the nearer opponent, in hopes of
splitting the melees".

The answer, recommended to every newbie, is to "run
like hell for the nearest bottleneck, so as to
guarantee taking on the opponents one at a time".

So, both discussion opponents here are dealing out
bad advice.

It's also well worth commenting that at this point
adults would have realized what was being discussed
wasn't matters of fact, but matters of opinion, and
exercised the "agree to disagree" meme so as to cut
the boredom level for others in reading rgrn.

